.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH octosnap-capture 1  OctoSnap 
.SH NAME
octosnap\-capture \- Take a screenshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBoctosnap capture\fR [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-mode\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-action\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-rect\fR] [\fB\-\-display\fR] [\fB\-\-freeze\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-freeze\fR] [\fB\-\-cursor\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-cursor\fR] [\fB\-\-timer\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Take a screenshot
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-mode\fR \fI<MODE>\fR [default: area]
What to capture
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
all\-in\-one: The overlay with its toolbar and the last selection restored
.IP \(bu 2
area: Drag out a region
.IP \(bu 2
window: Pick a window
.IP \(bu 2
fullscreen: The whole monitor under the pointer
.IP \(bu 2
previous\-area: The last selection again, with no overlay
.IP \(bu 2
self\-timer: Select a region, then capture after a countdown
.RE
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-action\fR \fI<ACTION>\fR
What to do with it, overriding the configured after\-capture actions
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
copy
.IP \(bu 2
save
.IP \(bu 2
annotate
.IP \(bu 2
upload
.IP \(bu 2
pin
.RE
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the capture to this file as a PNG, or to standard output with `\-`, once it is taken, and do nothing else with it: no card, no copy, no save
.TP
\fB\-\-rect\fR \fI<X,Y,W,H>\fR
Skip the overlay and capture exactly this region, as logical x,y,width,height
.TP
\fB\-\-display\fR \fI<CONNECTOR>\fR
Which monitor, by connector name. See `octosnap monitors`
.TP
\fB\-\-freeze\fR
Freeze the screen while selecting, overriding the setting
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-freeze\fR
Do not freeze the screen, overriding the setting
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR
Include the pointer, overriding the setting
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cursor\fR
Exclude the pointer, overriding the setting
.TP
\fB\-\-timer\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Countdown in seconds. Implies \-\-mode self\-timer
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
